# Line endings.
#
# WHAT THIS FIXES
#   push.ps1 was printing one of these per touched file, every push:
#
#     warning: in the working copy of 'server-v2/econ-calendar-discord.js',
#     LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it
#
#   That is `core.autocrlf=true` on the Windows laptop. Git stores LF in the
#   repo, then rewrites it to CRLF on checkout, and warns every time it is about
#   to. Nothing was wrong — it is pure noise, and it has nothing to do with
#   owner-vite, v3, or any build.
#
# WHY .gitattributes RATHER THAN A CONFIG FLIP
#   .gitattributes OVERRIDES core.autocrlf and travels with the repo, so the
#   laptop, the VPS and every Docker build agree without anyone running a
#   `git config` on a new machine. Everything here is built in Linux containers,
#   so LF in the working copy is also what the images actually get — a file can
#   no longer round-trip through a CRLF checkout and come back as a whole-file
#   diff with zero real changes.
#
# ONE-TIME, after this lands (safe — most files are already LF in the index):
#   git add --renormalize .
#   git commit -m "chore: normalize line endings to LF"

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts — these want CRLF in the working copy.
*.ps1   text eol=crlf
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf

# Binary — never converted, never diffed.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
*.webp          binary
*.avif          binary
*.mp4           binary
*.mov           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.jar           binary
*.zip           binary
*.gz            binary
*.tgz           binary
*.tar           binary
*.7z            binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
*.ttf           binary
*.otf           binary
*.eot           binary
*.db            binary
*.sqlite        binary
*.sqlite3       binary
*.bundle        binary
*.traineddata   binary

# Generated — keep them out of diffs and out of merge conflicts.
package-lock.json   linguist-generated -diff
